      {
        "name": "every-great-story-starts-with-a-spark-of-ambition--picture-an-entrepreneur-sitting-at-a-desk-late-at-night--looking-at-a-brilliant-new-product-or-service-they-ve-built--they-know-it-s-good--they-know-the-market-needs-it--but-to-launch-it-into-the-world--they-think-they-just-need-one-small-thing--a-logo--they-treat-the-logo-like-a-golden-ticket--if-they-can-just-get-a-nice-icon--everything-else-will-magically-fall-into-place--this-is-where-the-protagonist-hits-an-invisible-wall--a-logo-in-isolation-is-like-an-beautiful-steering-wheel-without-a-car-attached-to-it--when-a-small-or-medium-sized-business-invests-in-just-a-standalone-logo--they-quickly-realize-the-harsh-truth-of-modern-marketing--the-logo-looks-great-on-a-business-card--but-doesn-t-scale-on-a-mobile-device--the-colors-don-t-translate-well-to-a-website-layout--the-messaging-feels-disconnected-when-they-try-to-run-a-social-media-ad-",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "size": {
          "w": 349,
          "h": 325
        },
        "content": "Every great story starts with a spark of ambition. Picture an entrepreneur sitting at a desk late at night, looking at a brilliant new product or service they’ve built. They know it’s good. They know the market needs it. But to launch it into the world, they think they just need one small thing: a logo.\nThey treat the logo like a golden ticket. If they can just get a nice icon, everything else will magically fall into place.\nThis is where the protagonist hits an invisible wall. A logo in isolation is like an beautiful steering wheel without a car attached to it.\nWhen a small or medium-sized business invests in just a standalone logo, they quickly realize the harsh truth of modern marketing:\nThe logo looks great on a business card, but doesn't scale on a mobile device.\nThe colors don't translate well to a website layout.\nThe messaging feels disconnected when they try to run a social media ad.",
        "styles": {
